            </Fragment>
          )}
        </section>
      )}
    </div>

    {/*
      Launcher and menu are siblings, not one nested pill. The launcher is the only
      fixture that holds the corner; the menu is a free-standing bar centred on the
      page. They were one element while the pill GREW out of the circle, and that
      coupling is what gave the open bar no position of its own — its left edge was
      wherever the item count left it, so the whole bar slid sideways whenever a
      capability-gated tool declared itself and the row changed width.

      Source order stays launcher-then-menu: it is the order a keyboard reader tabs
      through and the order the a11y tree reports, and it is now free of any layout
      duty, since neither element's position is expressed as "next to the other one".
    */}
    {/*
      The Listen mark: the always-visible icon beside the launcher that says where the
      voice is, and whose tap folds the mini-player beside it in and out. Inert markup:
      listenPanel.ts writes its form (`data-state`) and its label on every state change,
      so nothing here carries a sentence of its own [LAW:one-source-of-truth]. The
      glyph is the Listen tool's, so the menu item and the mark can never draw the voice
      two ways. Present exactly when the Listen panel is, and shown by CSS only once the
